  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Concept**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the conceptual underpinnings for \"Glyph GVPH.\" The aim is to capture a premium feel, like an exclusive club for book lovers. The aesthetic should be vibrant, deep, and live - conjuring visual richness. The name, \"Glyph GVPH,\" should resonate with a sense of exclusivity.\n\n\n**Refining the Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now integrating horoscopes and zodiac elements. The visual design will be compartmentalized, with a liquid glass aesthetic for a premium feel. Currently, I\'m working with a split layout with a dark/lavender celestial theme. I need to boost the \"expensive\" feel, refine the layout to accommodate horoscopes, and enhance the glass effect. I\'m focusing on the typography and color palette to achieve a more vibrant yet sophisticated look.\n\nI\'m aiming for deep blacks, rich lavenders, and high contrast with bright glowing accents. I\'m keeping `Poppins` and `Source Serif 4`, but I am adjusting sizes and weights to look more editorial. The goal is to make the glass effect appear polished and etched. The current working name is \"GLYPH / GVPH\".\n\n\n**Restructuring the Panels**\n\nI\'m now implementing structural changes to `src/App.tsx`. The left panel requires an update to accommodate horoscopes. I\'m considering a tabbed interface (\"Library\" vs. \"Astrology\") or a bento-box style modular grid. I\'m leaning toward modular glass cards for a cleaner, more organized aesthetic. The layout will include a logo, tabbed access to a book library and horoscope section, and selectors for zodiac readings. I also need to begin constructing the components that will comprise the \"HoroscopePanel\".\n\n\n**Implementing the Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a new file to handle Zodiac, Chinese Zodiac, and readings. I\'ve updated the celestial background to be more vivid and deep, with glowing orbs. I also need to add horoscope data and update the App\'s state management, leaning toward a bento layout. I\'m actively drafting zodiac and Chinese zodiac details. The goal is to make the `liquid-glass` classes super premium by refining box shadows, borders, and backlighting.\n\n\n**Developing the UX**\n\nI\'m now focusing on branding and the exclusive club feel of \"YPH GVPH.\" I\'m incorporating words like \"Archive,\" \"Vault,\" \"Initiate,\" and \"Patron\" to boost the concept. The new layout will utilize a dashboard-style bento grid for the menu on the left, while a 3D book or Zodiac wheel will occupy the right.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m writing the code for `src/data.ts`, starting with simple Zodiac data and Chinese Zodiac signs. Then, I will write the code for `src/components/HoroscopePanel.tsx` using glass cards for Western Zodiac selection, daily/yearly readings, and Chinese Zodiac alignment. In `App.tsx`, I\'ll set the title as \"GLYPH // GVPH\" with a subtitle and update the left panel for the header.\n\n\n**Implementing the Glass**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the glass effect within the project. I will be updating `index.css` to achieve the desired look. I also need to use text abbreviations for the Zodiac signs since there aren\'t specific zodiac icons in Lucide. I\'m aiming for a balance of premium whitespace and thin borders with subtle metallic or glass sheens using Source Serif 4 and wide-tracked sans-serifs for a luxurious feel. The background will have deep purples with bright glowing orbs.\n\n\n**Refining the Framework**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the framework, starting with `src/data.ts` to add Astro data. I\'m concurrently working on creating `HoroscopePanel.tsx`, updating `CelestialBackground.tsx`, and updating `App.tsx`. I am aiming for deep, rich palettes, animations and vibrant rotating gradients. The HoroscopePanel is envisioned to have a chic UI.\n\n\n**Constructing the Selectors**\n\nI\'m now implementing the grid of selectors within `App.tsx`. The recent progress focuses on building the main frame with large, rounded glass panels, resulting in a premium feel. The layout includes a celestial background, a left panel for branding and content with tabs, and a right panel intended for a 3D stage or visualizer, which remains hidden on smaller screens. The liquid-glass effect is emphasized throughout, adding a distinct branding.\n\n\n**Enhancing the \"Glass\"**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the liquid glass effect, aiming for a high-end application feel. I\'m adding a subtle white border and noise texture overlays for the glass elements to achieve a luxurious effect. I\'ll also refine custom scrollbars to have a premium feel. The data, background, panel, and 3D book will also be made to look more elite.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 22
      nanos: 705437001
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
