  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Zodiac Mappings**\n\nI\'m currently focused on replacing `data.ts` with comprehensive Zodiac mappings, encompassing both Western and Chinese systems. My goal is an exhaustive, accurate matching. Next, I plan to tackle `index.css`, with a view to enhancing the visual aesthetics by working on colors and a glass effect. I will then edit `CelestialBackground.tsx` to add rotating, vivid, glowing gradients.\n\n\n**Designing New Panel Structure**\n\nI\'m now completely redesigning `App.tsx` with modular, glass-paneled interfaces. The left side will feature tab navigation for \"The Vault\" and \"The Oracle.\" \"The Vault\" will display books, while \"The Oracle\" will house the new horoscope feature. I\'ve also begun creating `src/components/HoroscopePanel.tsx` to get this done. Concurrently, I\'ve re-engaged with the `data.ts` update to include a flexible approach to Chinese Zodiac integration, allowing users to select either their Western or Chinese zodiac independently for synergy analysis.\n\n\n**Refining Alignment Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the logic for the horoscope feature. My current focus is integrating both Western and Chinese zodiacs, allowing users to select their Western sign first and see a corresponding \"Chinese Zodiac Alignment\" display below. I\'m thinking of showing curated matches or providing an option for secondary Chinese zodiac selection. I\'m updating `data.ts` to reflect the new data structure, including daily and yearly readings.\n\n\n"
