  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining the Core Concept**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core of this project. My focus is entirely on removing the \"GVPH,\" cultish language, and other unwanted branding. I\'ve also locked down the app name as \"glyph.\" (lowercase with a period). I\'m visualizing interactive blending to create the background.\n\n\n**Prioritizing & Refining Elements**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the key elements. The \"astro\" theme is now light lavender and gray, a minimalist change. The horoscope feature is demoted to a button, while reading is now front and center, with a levitating 3D book in the hero section. I\'ve started updating the CSS variables and CelestialBackground.tsx to reflect the new color scheme. I\'m removing the heavy purple shadows.\n\n\n**Implementing the UI Changes**\n\nI\'m now in the thick of implementation. The color palette is shifting to muted lavenders and grays. I\'m focusing on cleaning up the layout, particularly the split view in `App.tsx`. The goal is a minimalist hero with the 3D book always visible on desktop. I\'m converting the horoscope panel into a button-triggered modal to streamline the UI. The 3D Book is coming along nicely, and I will be looking to adjust shadow colors.\n\n\n**Simplifying Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the interactive elements. My focus is now on lighter, minimalist liquid glass effects. I\'m modifying CelestialBackground.tsx to create a parallax effect based on mouse position using grayscale and muted lavenders. The `App.tsx` layout is being refactored to prioritize the 3D book on the right, and the horoscope panel is moving to a modal button. I will ensure data colors don\'t clash, and then implement the modal overlay.\n\n\n**Implementing Code Changes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the code changes. I\'ve removed the tabs and moved the horoscope feature to a modal, triggered by a button. The left column of `App.tsx` now features books and categories, with the 3D book stage on the right. I\'m focusing on the parallax effect in `CelestialBackground.tsx` using mousemove and spring motion. I\'m updating the colors to grayscale and lavender and creating the `HoroscopeOverlay.tsx` to wrap the panel in a modal.\n\n\n**Implementing Modal Integration**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in coding. I\'ve decided whether to move the existing content into `HoroscopeOverlay.tsx` and have started editing `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve implemented a `showHoroscope` boolean instead of the previous `activeTab`. The logo is now \"glyph.\", and the layout now prioritizes the library and 3D book display. I\'ve also implemented a subtle \"Horoscope\" button at the bottom. I\'m focusing on refining the theme with soft lavender. I\'m beginning work on `src/index.css` for glass refinements. I am starting to implement the parallax effect within `CelestialBackground.tsx`, and need to import `useEffect`, `motion`, `useSpring`, and `useMotionValue`.\n\n\n**Refining Parallax Implementation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the parallax effect within `CelestialBackground.tsx`. I\'ve implemented a `HoroscopeOverlay.tsx` file for a modal component, and I\'ve begun to convert the `HoroscopePanel.tsx` component into a modal overlay. I\'m focusing on layout restructuring within `src/App.tsx`, and I\'m importing `useEffect`, `motion`, `useSpring`, and `useMotionValue` to achieve the desired effect.\n\n\n**Adjusting Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now refining the parallax effect, ensuring smooth mouse tracking within `CelestialBackground.tsx`. I\'m starting work on cleaning up the parallax effect code and optimizing its color, to be consistent with the other backgrounds, but subtle. Also I\'m focusing on the implementation details for the `HoroscopeOverlay.tsx` file for a modal component, and I\'ve begun to convert the `HoroscopePanel.tsx` component into a modal overlay.\n\n\n"
