    thinking: "**Rethinking the Interface**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in redesigning the \"Glyph\" app as a landing page for \"Prisma.\" My focus is on making the interface feel more lively and natural, paying close attention to the provided prompt. I\'m exploring different layouts to best highlight \"Prisma\'s\" key features.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Goal**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core request: transforming \"Glyph\" with \"Prisma\'s\" aesthetic. It appears the goal is to merge \"Prisma\'s\" design with \"Glyph\'s\" existing functionalities, potentially using a Prisma-style page as the landing page, or applying Prisma\'s look throughout. This is an exciting challenge!\n\n\n**Integrating Design Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now focused on weaving \"Prisma\'s\" visual style, suggested by the prompt, into the existing \"Glyph\" functionality. The challenge lies in integrating the \"Prisma\" landing page with the app\'s core features like the vault, oracle, and 3D book. I\'m considering a unified application structure, maybe with a hero section inspired by \"Prisma\" leading into the app\'s components, making sure to keep the app\'s essential features, as suggested in the prompt.\n\n\n**Defining the Integration**\n\nI\'m now determining how to blend Prisma\'s landing page elements with Glyph\'s functionality. I\'m thinking of a landing page with a video hero, \'About\' text, and a \'Features\' section, inspired by Prisma\'s prompt. Then, I can add an \"Enter Library\" button that links to Glyph\'s existing e-reading app, ensuring no existing features are lost, as the user requested.\n\n\n**Implementing the Landing Page**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on recreating the Prisma landing page as requested, but maybe rebranding it. I\'m thinking about integrating an e-reader function. I\'ll make the landing page the default route, using state to switch between the landing page and app view. I\'ve installed the specified fonts (Almarai and Instrument Serif) and updated `index.css`. Next up: building a `LandingPage` component that perfectly reflects the Prisma prompt.\n\n\n**Constructing the Landing Page**\n\nI\'m now diving into the creation of `LandingPage.tsx` using the provided video and icon resources, integrating everything within the app. I plan to build the structure with the hero section, the about section, and the features section. I will then use `App.tsx` to conditionally render the `LandingPage` component or the main app view, maintaining the requested flexibility.\n\n\n"
