    user_response: "Add a \'Reading Progress\' dashboard inside the ReaderOverlay that displays estimated reading time remaining, total chapters completed, and a reading streak counter for the user.\n\nAdd a background audio toggle that plays subtle, atmospheric ambient deep-space soundscapes in the Library view to enhance the immersive experience.\n\n\n\nThis is amazing work, but I want you to make it seem like more of a reading app. Instead of the guy holding a laptop, make him hold a book, sitting on a bench, looking over the cliff, as if he\'s lost in reading the book over the cliff.\n\nAfter we scroll back and click any of the buttons on the left-hand side, make it a horoscope, deep insight button, so that we can dive into the horoscope of the day for the user, as well as other zodiacs.\n\nOn the right-hand side, keep it as the access to the libraries. So when we enter the right-side button, the book app takes us to the cliff app, and also make it a bit better, like the landing page because only the landing page is good right now. The cliff landing page also needs some work. Make them both resemble similar to each other.\n\nGive me the finished product. Also, make sure that I have access to a lot of different books, so I can search for a book title and get access to it and read it and download it, and keep it saved in my book gallery, the cliff gallery. And I can always come back to that book, and it also keeps a tab of how much book I have read and where to start off from now. Gives me a summary of the book if I need on the bottom of the page, and also has a cute little bookmark."
    items {
      text: "Add a \'Reading Progress\' dashboard inside the ReaderOverlay that displays estimated reading time remaining, total chapters completed, and a reading streak counter for the user.\n\nAdd a background audio toggle that plays subtle, atmospheric ambient deep-space soundscapes in the Library view to enhance the immersive experience.\n\n\n\nThis is amazing work, but I want you to make it seem like more of a reading app. Instead of the guy holding a laptop, make him hold a book, sitting on a bench, looking over the cliff, as if he\'s lost in reading the book over the cliff.\n\nAfter we scroll back and click any of the buttons on the left-hand side, make it a horoscope, deep insight button, so that we can dive into the horoscope of the day for the user, as well as other zodiacs.\n\nOn the right-hand side, keep it as the access to the libraries. So when we enter the right-side button, the book app takes us to the cliff app, and also make it a bit better, like the landing page because only the landing page is good right now. The cliff landing page also needs some work. Make them both resemble similar to each other.\n\nGive me the finished product. Also, make sure that I have access to a lot of different books, so I can search for a book title and get access to it and read it and download it, and keep it saved in my book gallery, the cliff gallery. And I can always come back to that book, and it also keeps a tab of how much book I have read and where to start off from now. Gives me a summary of the book if I need on the bottom of the page, and also has a cute little bookmark."
    }
  }
}
