  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User\'s Vision**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics. The request to integrate a \'Reading Progress\' dashboard within `ReaderOverlay` is becoming clearer. I\'m focusing on the implementation details for the estimated reading time remaining, total chapters read, and reading streak counter. Furthermore, I\'ve got a handle on the background audio toggle for the Library.\n\n\n**Refining the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual updates. I\'ve decided to replace the hero video with a generated image. My primary approach involves using image generation to create a cinematic asset depicting someone reading a book on a cliff, completely lost in the story. Alternatively, I can provide a prompt for image generation, leaning towards using the `default_api:generate_image` tool if possible. I\'m also planning to explore the possibility of using an existing video if it is available.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Features for Landing Page**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing key features for the landing page. My focus has shifted to ensuring access to many different mock books and ensuring the search functionality actually works with them. I\'m also thinking about incorporating mock download functionality and saving books to a \"cliff gallery\". Tracking reading progress is important, along with a book summary and a cute bookmark. I need to integrate these elements to improve the page\'s quality.\n\n\n**Implementing Navigation Changes**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on navigation updates. I\'m focusing on \"Horoscope/Insights\" and the \"Library\". I plan to add an ambient audio toggle and \"Save to Gallery\" within the Library view. I\'m also preparing to integrate \"Reading Progress\", a book \"Summary\", and a \"Bookmark\" UI. I will also incorporate similar font, colors and styling of the landing page to other components like `AppContent`. The plan includes navigation links reflecting these two paths.\n\n\n**Mapping the Implementation Steps**\n\nI\'m now outlining the steps to make sure I create something beautiful. First, I will generate the hero image, and then update the data to contain book summaries, and progress. Next I\'ll work on the global state in `App.tsx` and build the `AppContent` UI. This will be split into `LibraryView` and `HoroscopeView` components for code clarity, I hope to have all components in the matching \"cliff\" theme. Finally I will update the `ReaderOverlay.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Image and Data**\n\nI\'m now generating the hero image using a cinematic prompt to get a moody shot of someone reading on a cliff. The goal is photorealistic quality with a cosmic starry background. Simultaneously, I\'m working to edit `/src/data.ts`, adding book summaries and estimated read times to the `Book` type. I\'ll integrate `lucide-react` icons for the bookmark and audio controls. The image generation call will happen alongside data edits, leveraging `default_api:generate_image` with a prompt.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 34
      nanos: 18254753
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
