  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Onboarding Process**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the onboarding flow. The core goal is clear: gather essential user data (DOB, age, name, sex) and offer them a color theme choice right at the start. I\'m also planning a Settings menu for later adjustments. The key will be making the process smooth.\n\n\n**Refining Functionality and Storage**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the \"Link Google Account\" button \342\200\223 top right next to search. I\'ll leverage the OAuth skill for Google integration, or if the UI is preferred, I\'ll build the UI first. The user\'s feedback about the non-functional search bar and buttons is prompting me to prioritize functionality. I\'m also addressing the database question, explaining how we can store data locally using `localStorage` since Firebase was declined, or discuss other options like a Node.js/Express server.\n\n\n**Implementing UI and State**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the UI implementation. The `userProfile` state is created for user data. I\'ll display an `OnboardingModal` if `!userProfile.name`, and a `SettingsModal` is planned behind a settings icon. Themes will dynamically change the animated background and I am defining CSS variables for various themes. I\'ve updated `App.tsx` and created the required modal components. Also, the UI rendering issue with the search bar is resolved! The application now correctly reflects search filters.\n\n\n**Revising Button Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on wiring up those non-functional buttons. My current plan is to use `localStorage` states like `savedBooks` to store user interactions with things like bookmarks and \"read extract\" functions. This way, I can make the UI more responsive.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Initiating Google OAuth**\n\nOkay, I\'m setting up Google OAuth. I need to call `set_up_oauth`. The requested scopes are for user profile and email. The UI title is now set to \"Use Google to sign in to your account\", and `userConfirmedInUI` is set to `false`. I must stop the conversation if this is set to false. Also, the layout changes were added!\n\n\n**Prioritizing OAuth Integration**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the Google OAuth flow. I thought I could build the UI and then handle OAuth, but the guidelines mandate an immediate stop after `set_up_oauth`. My plan is to incorporate the UI updates and then include a clear prompt explaining the required OAuth setup. I\'m aiming to trigger the OAuth prompt as the final action in this round.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Persistence**\n\nRight now, I\'m working to make user data stick around! I\'m creating the `UserProfile` model and adding `localStorage` hooks in `App.tsx` for that, as well as themes. I need to make sure the search is still working correctly. I\'m focusing on applying theme colors to those background blobs. Onboarding and Settings modals are planned, with the first collecting the standard user data (name, DOB, age, sex, theme), and the latter letting the user edit their profile and change the current theme. I will also incorporate the Google Auth button next to the search bar. Finally, I\'ll build `hooks/useLocalStorage.ts`.\n\n\n**Constructing Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now building the fundamental component structure. I\'ve created `components/Onboarding.tsx` and `components/Settings.tsx`, and I\'m updating `App.tsx` to integrate these, along with state for `userProfile`. I will also apply themes to the background blobs and ensure \"Bookmark\" buttons modify a `savedBooks` array. \"Read Now\" should now open the `ReaderOverlay`. \"View all\" will either do nothing or scroll. My next focus is handling the Google OAuth tool. I\'ll provide an explanation about `localStorage` as a lightweight alternative to Firebase for data storage. I am also checking `src/App.tsx` for `filteredBooks` state.\n\n\n**Verifying Search Functionality**\n\nI\'m now carefully reviewing search functionality. My initial analysis indicates search should work, based on the code in `filteredBooks.map`. The input field is tied to `setSearchQuery`. I need to ensure the UI updates correctly with search results. My plan is to add a `useLocalStorage` hook and verify bookmark interactions within the layout. I\'m focusing on refining the theme system, mapping chosen themes to color schemes.\n\n\n"
